# GitHub Pages custom domain template.
#
# To use a custom domain:
#   1. Rename this file to "CNAME" (no extension), in the repository ROOT,
#      and put your domain on a single line, e.g.:
#          freeapihub.example.com
#   2. At your DNS provider, create a CNAME record pointing that hostname to
#      <your-username>.github.io
#   3. In your repository: Settings -> Pages -> Custom domain -> enter the
#      same domain and save. Wait for the DNS check to pass.
#   4. IMPORTANT: update config/site.json so the generated canonical URLs,
#      sitemap and robots.txt match your domain:
#          "site_url": "https://freeapihub.example.com"
#          "site_url_path": ""
#   5. Re-run the "Deploy Site" workflow (Actions -> Deploy Site -> Run).
#
# Without this file the site works fine on the default
# https://<username>.github.io/<repository>/ address.
